  "worked_solution": "First, we move the constant term to the right-hand side, factor the coefficient of the quadratic term, and complete the square on the left-hand side.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6{z}^{2}+10z-1 & =0 \\\\ 6{z}^{2}+10z & =1 \\\\ 6({z}^{2}+\\frac{5}{3}z) & =1 \\\\ 6[{z}^{2}+2\\cdot \\frac{5}{6}\\cdot z+{(\\frac{5}{6})}^{2}-{(\\frac{5}{6})}^{2}] & =1 \\\\ 6[{(z+\\frac{5}{6})}^{2}-{(\\frac{5}{6})}^{2}] & =1 \\\\ 6[{(z+\\frac{5}{6})}^{2}-\\frac{25}{36}] & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we expand the brackets, and write the equation in the required form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6{(z+\\frac{5}{6})}^{2}-6\\cdot \\frac{25}{36} & =1 \\\\ 6{(z+\\frac{5}{6})}^{2}-\\frac{25}{6} & =1 \\\\ 6{(z+\\frac{5}{6})}^{2} & =\\frac{31}{6}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $p=\\frac{5}{6}$ and $q=\\frac{31}{6}.$ Finally,\n\n$$\np+q=\\frac{5}{6}+\\frac{31}{6}=\\frac{36}{6}=6.\n$$",
